{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785088829,"nonce":"o7pE67lkf6d3A8ssZ6oJkpRMmhY=","title":"Two tiers, two policies, so eviction can never break a promise:","message":"- workspace service (warm): bounded by SPACE, LRU eviction, carries NO\n  promise — a miss is slower, never wrong.\n- object storage (cold): bounded by TIME, a retention TTL, exactly as\n  Artifacts already are. This is the guarantee users are given.\n\nPlus: manual PIN (\"keep this Run's workspaces\") for investigations, and\ngraceful degradation — expired inputs widen a rerun's scope rather than\nfailing. Rerun affordances must say which they are (\"Rerun this step\" vs\n\"Inputs expired — this re-runs from clone\"), per ADR-0027's rule that smart\nnever means mysterious.\n\nRelates to ADR-0050 (retention \u0026 GC).","files":null}]}